---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: whats-new/index.html
bodyClass: whats-new-page
pageTitle: What’s new in Dekopon v0.2.0
pageDescription: Version 0.2.0 brings secure agent tools, fine-grained permissions, auditing, and OpenTelemetry to hardware as small as a Raspberry Pi.
ogType: article
---
<section class="release-hero">
  <div class="release-hero-mesh" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
  <div class="shell release-hero-grid">
    <div class="release-hero-copy">
      <p class="release-eyebrow reveal"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ whatsNew.hero.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><span>{{ whatsNew.hero.version }}</span>{{ whatsNew.hero.title }}</h1>
      <p class="release-lede reveal reveal-delay-2">{{ whatsNew.hero.lede }}</p>
      <div class="release-actions reveal reveal-delay-3">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#get-v020">Get v0.2.0 <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="{{ whatsNew.hero.releaseUrl }}">GitHub release <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="release-card reveal reveal-delay-2" aria-label="v0.2.0 release details">
      <div class="release-card-top">
        <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i> Current release</span>
        <code>{{ whatsNew.hero.revision }}</code>
      </div>
      <strong>{{ whatsNew.hero.version }}</strong>
      <p>Released <time datetime="2026-08-16">16 August 2026</time></p>
      <div class="release-command" data-copy-group>
        <span aria-hidden="true">$</span>
        <code>{{ whatsNew.hero.install }}</code>
        <button type="button" data-copy="{{ whatsNew.hero.install }}" aria-label="Copy install command">
          <span class="copy-label">Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <a href="{{ whatsNew.hero.sourceUrl }}">See the code for this release <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <div class="shell release-metrics reveal reveal-delay-4">
    {% for metric in whatsNew.metrics %}
      <div><strong>{{ metric.value }}</strong><span>{{ metric.label }}</span></div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="release-summary section" aria-labelledby="release-summary-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="release-section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-kicker purple">The short version</span>
        <h2 id="release-summary-title">The release in three points.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Your agents can now run multi-step tools, ask for tightly limited network access, and show you what happened from prompt to provider.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="release-highlight-grid">
      {% for highlight in whatsNew.highlights %}
        <article class="release-highlight reveal{% if loop.index > 1 %} reveal-delay-{{ loop.index - 1 }}{% endif %}">
          <div class="release-highlight-top"><span>{{ highlight.number }}</span><small>{{ highlight.kicker }}</small></div>
          <h3>{{ highlight.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ highlight.body }}</p>
          <ul>
            {% for point in highlight.points %}<li>{{ point }}</li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="release-path-section" aria-labelledby="release-path-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="release-path-heading">
      <div><span class="section-kicker mint">One secure path</span><h2 id="release-path-title">The agent asks. The broker decides.</h2></div>
      <p>The request contains the action, not the permission. The broker verifies the local caller and checks your rule before one limited provider call can run.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="release-path" aria-label="How Dekopon checks one agent request">
      {% for step in whatsNew.path %}
        <li><span>0{{ loop.index }}</span><strong>{{ step.name }}</strong><small>{{ step.detail }}</small></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="release-details section" aria-labelledby="release-details-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="release-section-heading release-details-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-kicker orange">Under the hood</span>
        <h2 id="release-details-title">What v0.2.0 brings.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The safe scripting tool cannot reach your operating system. The runner cannot approve an action. Providers cannot exceed the host access and limits you give them.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="release-change-list">
      {% for change in whatsNew.changes %}
        <article class="release-change reveal">
          <div class="release-change-index"><span>0{{ loop.index }}</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
          <div>
            <small>{{ change.tag }}</small>
            <h3>{{ change.title }}</h3>
            <p>{{ change.body }}</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="{{ change.link.href }}">{{ change.link.label }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <aside class="release-telemetry reveal" aria-label="Measured OpenObserve storage">
      <div><span>OpenObserve · physical allocation</span><strong>{{ whatsNew.telemetry.value }}</strong><small>{{ whatsNew.telemetry.title }}</small></div>
      <div><p>{{ whatsNew.telemetry.body }}</p><small>{{ whatsNew.telemetry.note }}</small></div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="release-install section" id="get-v020" aria-labelledby="release-install-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="release-section-heading release-install-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-kicker mint">Published on crates.io</span>
        <h2 id="release-install-title">Pick your starting point.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Install any of the three command-line tools on its own. You can also download an attested build of the main CLI from GitHub.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="release-package-grid">
      {% for package in whatsNew.packages %}
        <article class="release-package reveal{% if loop.index > 1 %} reveal-delay-{{ loop.index - 1 }}{% endif %}">
          <div><code>{{ package.name }}</code><span>{{ package.role }}</span></div>
          <p>{{ package.body }}</p>
          <div class="release-package-command" data-copy-group>
            <code>{{ package.command }}</code>
            <button type="button" data-copy="{{ package.command }}" aria-label="Copy {{ package.name }} install command"><span class="copy-label">Copy</span></button>
          </div>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="release-scope section" aria-labelledby="release-scope-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="release-section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-kicker purple">Where v0.2.0 stands</span>
        <h2 id="release-scope-title">Ready to explore. Not production-ready yet.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The local permission path works today. Broker-managed provider credentials, stronger audit anchoring, multi-tenant networking, and production hardening still come next.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="release-scope-grid">
      <article class="release-scope-card current reveal">
        <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i> Current in v0.2.0</span>
        <ul>{% for item in whatsNew.scope.current %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      </article>
      <article class="release-scope-card next reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i> Coming next</span>
        <ul>{% for item in whatsNew.scope.next %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <article class="previous-release reveal">
      <div><span>Previous release</span><strong>{{ whatsNew.previous.version }}</strong></div>
      <div><h3>{{ whatsNew.previous.title }}</h3><p>{{ whatsNew.previous.body }}</p></div>
      <a href="{{ whatsNew.previous.url }}" aria-label="View the v0.1.0 release">View 0.1 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="release-closing">
  <div class="shell release-closing-inner">
    <div><span class="section-kicker mint">v0.2.0 is available now</span><h2>Install it.<br>Take it for a spin.</h2></div>
    <div><p>See every change on GitHub, or open the Tech Almanac for a clear tour of the code that ships.</p><div class="release-actions"><a class="button button-white" href="{{ whatsNew.hero.releaseUrl }}">Full release notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-ghost" href="/almanac/">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
